## UI standards

- Distinctive, editorial, accessible (WCAG AA). Avoid generic AI-purple gradients and system-font sameness.
- Typography: Syne + Manrope (already in project). Motion purposeful; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Progress must feel **alive**: SSE detail lines, stall hints during long LLM calls, honest batch counters.

## Ops checklist after schema/API changes

1. `pnpm --filter api exec prisma migrate deploy` (or `pnpm db:migrate:deploy`)
2. `pnpm --filter @aptos-translate/contracts build` if contracts changed
3. Kill `:3000`/`:3001` if needed, restart `pnpm dev`, one-shot `curl` verify
4. Never ask the user to free ports or wait on terminals

## Quality bar vs legacy v1

| Must preserve | v1 mechanism | v2 location |
|---------------|--------------|-------------|
| Row alignment | id/ix JSON validation | `llm-response-alignment.ts` |
| Dual LLM | translate then judge | orchestrator + Bedrock services |
| Batch retry | whole batch on any failure | targeted sid retry (max 3 rounds) |
| Never shrink arrays | placeholders on hard fail | alignment throw → retry |
| Domain prompts | POS glossary + LANG_CONFIG | `prompt-builder.ts`, `lang-config.ts` |

When translation quality regresses, compare behavior to `aptos-translateai/llms/gemini_llm.py` and `core/processor.py` before weakening validation.
